/-
The solution of Lean stage L2 (`local certificate generator.md`). It is
stage L1's solution (`local certificate generator`) with the
library's other certificates added: for r = 3 (mod 4) each main theorem is
`Opn.sound` on the certificate; for r = 1 (mod 4) it is
`Opn.sound_given`, which takes the cited fact `NotSpecial r` as a
hypothesis. Lean's kernel checks each certificate by evaluating
`T2.checkCert`. The terms are written by `local certificate generator` with
`certificate generator`.
-/


@[expose] public section

namespace OpnCerts

def EqualExponents (r N : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∃ π : ℕ, π.Prime ∧
    ∀ q : ℕ, q.Prime → q ∣ N → q ≠ π → N.factorization q = r - 1

